  "tasks": {
    "T3": {
      "text": "The Poisson distribution models the number of events in a fixed interval when events occur independently at a constant average rate. P(X >= 5) is the complement of P(X <= 4), so it is 1 minus the cumulative distribution function at 4. P(X = 8) needs the probability mass function, not the cdf.",
